  "caption": "Quinn bowled in the nets, at school, at club and in the backyard. Then one side of the back started to grumble, and the shoulder joined in.\n\nFast bowling bends and twists the lower back under big force, and boundary throws load the shoulder. Sudden jumps in bowling or throwing, often at the start of the season, are a common trigger.\n\nWhat often helps: count every ball you bowl, build up gradually through preseason, strengthen your trunk, hips, shoulders and hamstrings, warm up properly, and wear your helmet.\n\nIf a young bowler has one-sided back pain, pain lasting a week or two, or pain that comes back after rest, get it checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
